        "title": "Freelancing Ki Duniya — Income Tax Ka Complete Guide (Part 2)",
        "content": "### Section 44ADA — Presumptive Taxation (Detailed)\n\nYeh freelancers ka FAVORITE section hai! 44ADA kya hai? Samajhte hain:\n\n**44ADA ka Magic:**\n- Government ne socha ki small professionals ko itna complex tax calculation mat karo\n- **50% of gross receipts** ko automatically deduct kar lo as \"expenses\"\n- Remaining 50% pe tax lagega\n- **Koi receipts, koi bills ki zaroorat nahi!**\n\n**Who Can Use 44ADA:**\n\n| Profession | Eligible? | Example |\n|------------|-----------|---------|\n| Freelance Writer | ✅ Yes | Priya (content writer) |\n| Graphic Designer | ✅ Yes | Amit (UI/UX designer) |\n| Web Developer | ✅ Yes | Sneha (full-stack dev) |\n| Consultant | ✅ Yes | Kunal (marketing consultant) |\n| Photographer | ✅ Yes | Meera (freelance photographer) |\n| CA/Lawyer/Doctor | ✅ Yes | Professionals |\n| Tutor/Coach | ✅ Yes | Aman (online tutor) |\n| Influencer | ✅ Yes | Social media creators |\n\n**Who CANNOT Use 44ADA:**\n- Anyone with income above ₹75 lakh (new limit)\n- Those who want to claim actual expenses (better deduction)\n- Those with multiple professions (different rules apply)\n\n**44ADA Calculation Example:**\n\n```\nPriya's Freelance Writing Income (FY 2025-26):\nGross Receipts: ₹8,00,000\n\nUnder 44ADA:\nAutomatic 50% Deduction: ₹4,00,000\nTaxable Income: ₹4,00,000\n\nTax Calculation (New Regime):\nUp to ₹3,00,000: NIL\n₹3,00,001 to ₹4,00,000: 5% of ₹1,00,000 = ₹5,000\nTotal Tax: ₹5,000\n\nBUT wait! Section 87A rebate: Since taxable income after deduction is ₹4,00,000, \nand new regime mein ₹7 lakh tak rebate milta hai, Priya ka tax = ZERO!\n```\n\n**When to Use 44ADA vs Actual Expenses:**\n\n| Situation | 44ADA Better? | Actual Expenses Better? |\n|-----------|---------------|------------------------|\n| Low expenses (10-20% of income) | ✅ Yes (50% deduction is more) | ❌ No |\n| High expenses (60-70% of income) | ❌ No (only 50% deduction) | ✅ Yes (can claim more) |\n| Want simplicity | ✅ Yes (no receipts needed) | ❌ No (need documentation) |\n| Income < ₹75 lakh | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |\n| Income > ₹75 lakh | ❌ No (not eligible) | ✅ Yes |\n\n**Rahul's Decision:**\nRahul earns ₹6 lakh/year freelancing. His actual expenses are only ₹80,000 (laptop EMI, internet, software). \n\n44ADA: ₹3,00,000 taxable (50% of ₹6L)\nActual: ₹5,20,000 taxable (₹6L - ₹80K)\n\nClearly, 44ADA is better for Rahul!\n\n### ITR-4 Filing for Freelancers — Step by Step\n\nITR-4 (Sugam) is for freelancers using presumptive taxation. Here's how to file:",
