        "title": "Freelancing Ki Duniya — Income Tax Ka Complete Guide (Part 3)",
        "content": "**Step 1: Gather Documents**\n- PAN card\n- Aadhaar card\n- Bank statements (all accounts)\n- Platform earnings statements (Upwork, Fiverr etc.)\n- Client invoices\n- TDS certificates (Form 16A)\n\n**Step 2: Calculate Total Income**\n```\nGross Freelance Receipts: ₹_______\nAdd: Other Income (interest, rent etc.): ₹_______\nTotal Income: ₹_______\n```\n\n**Step 3: Apply 44ADA**\n```\nPresumptive Income (50% of receipts): ₹_______\nOR Actual Expenses (if opted out of 44ADA): ₹_______\n```\n\n**Step 4: Claim Deductions**\n- Section 80C (up to ₹1.5 lakh)\n- Section 80D (health insurance)\n- Section 80CCD(1B) (NPS)\n- Section 80GG (rent)\n\n**Step 5: Calculate Tax**\n- Apply slab rates\n- Add cess (4%)\n- Subtract TDS already deducted\n- Subtract advance tax paid\n\n**Step 6: File Online**\n- Login to incometax.gov.in\n- Select ITR-4\n- Fill details\n- Verify with Aadhaar OTP\n- Submit!\n\n**Deadline:** July 31st every year. Late filing penalty: ₹1,000 to ₹5,000.\n\n### GST Registration for Freelancers\n\nGST (Goods and Services Tax) freelancers ke liye important hai:\n\n| Criteria | Status |\n|----------|--------|\n| Annual turnover < ₹20 lakh | GST registration optional |\n| Annual turnover > ₹20 lakh | GST registration MANDATORY |\n| Interstate supply (different state clients) | GST registration MANDATORY |\n| Online/digital services to clients outside India | GST registration MANDATORY |\n\n**When to Register:**\n- If you cross ₹20 lakh threshold\n- If you want to claim Input Tax Credit\n- If big clients require GST invoice\n- If you want to look professional\n\n**When to Skip:**\n- Income < ₹20 lakh and no plans to grow\n- All clients are in same state and don't need GST invoice\n- You're just starting and want to keep things simple\n\n**HSN/SAC Codes for Freelancing:**\n\n| Service | SAC Code | GST Rate |\n|---------|----------|----------|\n| IT Services | 998314 | 18% |\n| Design Services | 998319 | 18% |\n| Content Writing | 998319 | 18% |\n| Consulting | 998319 | 18% |\n| Photography | 998319 | 18% |\n| Tutoring (online) | 999220 | 18% |\n\n**Aman's GST Journey:**\nAman (22, Bangalore) started freelancing web development. First year income: ₹8 lakh. No GST needed. Second year: ₹25 lakh. GST registration mandatory! He registered, started charging 18% GST from clients. Now he claims ITC on his laptop, software, and internet bills. Net GST cost: Much lower than 18%!\n\n---",
