        "id": "13-3-1",
        "topicId": "13-3",
        "topicTitle": "GST Guide for Freelancers — Kab Register Karna Hai",
        "cardIndex": 1,
        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "GST Guide for Freelancers — Kab Register Karna Hai",
        "content": "GST freelancers ke liye ek maze ka game hai — samajh lo toh paisa bachao, nahi samjhe toh paisa jaaye! Let's break it down.\n\n### GST Threshold — ₹20 Lakh Ka Rule\n\n| Your Annual Turnover | GST Registration | GST Collection |\n|----------------------|------------------|----------------|\n| < ₹20 lakh | Optional | Not required |\n| ₹20 lakh - ₹1.5 crore | Mandatory | 18% on invoices |\n| > ₹1.5 crore | Mandatory + Audit | 18% + separate rules |\n\n**Important:** ₹20 lakh threshold includes ALL income — freelancing + any other business income. Agar tumhara total ₹20 lakh cross ho raha hai, GST register karo!\n\n### When to Register vs When to Skip\n\n**Register for GST When:**\n1. Income > ₹20 lakh (mandatory)\n2. Big clients (corporates) insist on GST invoice\n3. You want to claim Input Tax Credit (ITC)\n4. Interstate clients (different state)\n5. Exporting services (zero-rated supply)\n\n**Skip GST When:**\n1. Income < ₹20 lakh\n2. All clients are individuals/small businesses\n3. You don't need ITC\n4. You're just starting out\n5. Administrative burden seems too much\n\n**Priya's Confusion:**\nPriya earns ₹18 lakh from writing. She thinks she doesn't need GST. But wait — she also sells online courses worth ₹5 lakh. Total: ₹23 lakh. GST mandatory! She didn't register, got notice from GST department. Penalty: ₹10,000 + interest. Lesson learned!\n\n### Input Tax Credit (ITC) — Paisa Bachao Ka Funda\n\nITC ka matlab hai: Jo GST tumne apne business expenses pe pay kiya, usse tum apni GST liability se kaat sakte ho.\n\n**Example:**\n```\nPriya charges ₹1,18,000 from client (₹1,00,000 + 18% GST)\nPriya's GST liability: ₹18,000\n\nBut Priya spent on:\n- Software subscription: ₹12,000 + ₹2,160 GST\n- Internet bill: ₹6,000 + ₹1,080 GST\n- Laptop: ₹50,000 + ₹9,000 GST\n- Co-working space: ₹24,000 + ₹4,320 GST\n\nTotal ITC Available: ₹2,160 + ₹1,080 + ₹9,000 + ₹4,320 = ₹16,560\n\nNet GST to pay: ₹18,000 - ₹16,560 = ₹1,440 only!\n```\n\n**What Qualifies for ITC:**\n\n| Expense | ITC Available? | Conditions |\n|---------|---------------|------------|\n| Laptop/Desktop | ✅ Yes | Must be used for business |\n| Software | ✅ Yes | Business-related |\n| Internet | ✅ Yes | Proportional to business use |\n| Phone | ✅ Yes | Proportional |\n| Office rent | ✅ Yes | If registered office |\n| Travel | ✅ Yes | Client meetings only |\n| Food/Entertainment | ❌ No | Blocked under GST |\n| Personal expenses | ❌ No | Not business-related |\n\n### GST Filing — Monthly vs Quarterly (QRMP)",
        "color": "#2563eb",
        "emoji": "💻",
        "interactiveType": "none"
