        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Advance Tax — Mahine Ka Paisa, Mahine Ka Tax (Part 2)",
        "content": "**Step 4: Calculate Tax**\n```\nApply slab rates\nAdd 4% cess\nSubtract TDS already deducted (if any)\n= Advance Tax Payable\n```\n\n**Step 5: Divide by Installments**\n```\n15% by June 15\n45% by September 15\n75% by December 15\n100% by March 15\n```\n\n### Online Payment Process (Challan 280)\n\n**Step 1:** Go to https://onlineservices.tin.gov.in\n**Step 2:** Select Challan 280\n**Step 3:** Fill details:\n- PAN\n- Assessment Year (next year)\n- Type of Payment: Advance Tax (100)\n- Mode of payment: Net Banking / Debit Card\n**Step 4:** Pay and save receipt\n**Step 5:** Note BSR code and challan number\n\n**Important:** Payment ka receipt zaroor save karo! ITR mein challan details bharni padti hain.\n\n### Interest Under Section 234B and 234C\n\nAgar advance tax nahi pay kiya ya kam pay kiya, toh interest lagta hai:\n\n**Section 234B (Default in Advance Tax):**\n- Agar advance tax < 90% of total tax liability\n- Interest: 1% per month on shortfall\n- Calculated from April 1 till date of payment\n\n**Section 234C (Deferment of Installments):**\n- Agar kisi installment mein kam pay kiya\n- Interest: 1% per month on shortfall\n- For 3 months (for each shortfall)\n\n**Aman's Penalty:**\nAman's total tax liability: ₹60,000\nHe paid: ₹30,000 (only 50%)\nShortfall: ₹30,000\nInterest 234B: ₹30,000 × 1% × 12 months = ₹3,600\nInterest 234C: ₹30,000 × 1% × 9 months = ₹2,700\nTotal Interest: ₹6,300\n\nOuch! That's extra money just for late payment!\n\n### How to Adjust TDS Against Advance Tax\n\nIf clients have deducted TDS, you can adjust it against advance tax:\n\n```\nTotal Tax Liability: ₹80,000\nTDS Deducted by Clients: ₹25,000\nAdvance Tax Payable: ₹55,000",
