        "title": "Expense Deductions — Kitna Bacha Sakte Ho",
        "content": "Freelancers ke liye expense deductions GOLD hai! Module 10 mein humne basic deductions dekhe, ab detailed dekhte hain freelancers ke liye kaun-kaun se expenses deductible hain.\n\n### Complete List of Deductible Expenses\n\n| Expense Category | Deductible? | How Much | Documentation Needed |\n|-----------------|-------------|----------|---------------------|\n| **Home Office** | | | |\n| Rent (proportional) | ✅ Yes | Based on space % | Rent receipts, agreement |\n| Electricity (proportional) | ✅ Yes | Based on usage % | Electricity bills |\n| Internet (proportional) | ✅ Yes | Based on usage % | Internet bills |\n| **Equipment** | | | |\n| Laptop/Desktop | ✅ Yes | Depreciation 40% | Purchase invoice |\n| Phone | ✅ Yes | Depreciation 40% | Purchase invoice |\n| Camera | ✅ Yes | Depreciation 40% | Purchase invoice |\n| Furniture | ✅ Yes | Depreciation 10% | Purchase invoice |\n| **Software** | | | |\n| Adobe CC | ✅ Yes | 100% | Subscription receipt |\n| Microsoft 365 | ✅ Yes | 100% | Subscription receipt |\n| Other tools | ✅ Yes | 100% | Subscription receipt |\n| **Professional** | | | |\n| Courses/Training | ✅ Yes | 100% | Course receipt |\n| Books/Publications | ✅ Yes | 100% | Purchase receipt |\n| Professional memberships | ✅ Yes | 100% | Membership receipt |\n| **Marketing** | | | |\n| Website hosting | ✅ Yes | 100% | Hosting receipt |\n| Domain name | ✅ Yes | 100% | Purchase receipt |\n| Advertising | ✅ Yes | 100% | Ad receipts |\n| **Operations** | | | |\n| Co-working space | ✅ Yes | 100% | Rent receipts |\n| Travel (client meetings) | ✅ Yes | 100% | Travel tickets, bills |\n| Phone bills | ✅ Yes | Proportional | Phone bills |\n| Office supplies | ✅ Yes | 100% | Purchase receipts |\n| **Financial** | | | |\n| Bank charges | ✅ Yes | 100 | Bank statement |\n| CA fees | ✅ Yes | 100% | CA invoice |\n| Professional tax | ✅ Yes | 100% | Payment receipt |\n\n### How to Maintain Expense Records\n\n**Rule #1: Har Expense Ka Record Rakho!**\n\n```\nEXPENSE TRACKING SYSTEM:\n\nDaily: Screenshot/photograph bills\nWeekly: Enter in spreadsheet/app\nMonthly: Categorize and review\nQuarterly: Summarize for tax planning\nAnnually: Finalize for ITR filing\n```\n\n**Priya's System:**\nPriya uses a simple Google Sheet:\n\n| Date | Expense | Category | Amount | GST | Bill Photo | Purpose |\n|------|---------|----------|--------|-----|------------|---------|\n| 15-Apr | Adobe CC | Software | ₹1,500 | ₹270 | IMG_001 | Design work |\n| 18-Apr | Internet | Utility | ₹1,200 | ₹216 | IMG_002 | Client work |\n| 22-Apr | Client meeting | Travel | ₹800 | ₹0 | IMG_003 | Mumbai client |\n\n### Which Expenses Need Bills vs Which Don't\n\n| Expense Type | Bill Required? | Alternative Proof |\n|--------------|---------------|-------------------|\n| Rent | ✅ Yes (Rent receipt) | Bank transfer statement |\n| Software | ✅ Yes (Email receipt) | Credit card statement |\n| Internet | ✅ Yes (Bill) | Bank statement |\n| Travel | ✅ Yes (Ticket) | UPI transaction |\n| Petty expenses (< ₹500) | ❌ No | Self-declaration + UPI |\n| Depreciation assets | ✅ Yes (Invoice) | Bank statement |\n\n**Amit's Trick:**\nAmit takes photos of all bills immediately. He has a WhatsApp group named \"Business Expenses\" where he sends photos daily. At month end, he categorizes everything. Smart!\n\n### Common Mistakes in Claiming Deductions\n\n| Mistake | Why It's Wrong | Correct Approach |\n|---------|---------------|------------------|\n| Claiming personal expenses | Not business-related | Only business-use portion |\n| No bills for expenses | Can't prove | Always maintain receipts |\n| Claiming 100% home rent | Need proportional | Calculate home office % |\n| Claiming full phone bill | Personal use included | Business-use proportion |\n| Wrong depreciation rate | IRS/CBIC rules | Follow prescribed rates |\n| Claiming without GST registration | ITC not available | Register first if needed |\n\n### Real Example: Content Writer's Expense Deduction\n\n**Rahul's Complete Expense Calculation:**\n\n```\nRAHUL WRITING SERVICES\nFY 2025-26\n\nGROSS INCOME: ₹10,00,000\n\nEXPENSES:\n\n1. HOME OFFICE (20% of home used for work)\n   Total home rent: ₹1,80,000\n   Deductible: ₹36,000 (20%)\n\n   Electricity: ₹18,000 × 20% = ₹3,600\n   Internet: ₹18,000 × 100% = ₹18,000 (fully used for work)\n\n2. EQUIPMENT\n   Laptop: ₹65,000 → 40% depreciation = ₹26,000\n   Phone: ₹25,000 → 40% depreciation = ₹10,000\n   Ergonomic chair: ₹15,000 → 10% depreciation = ₹1,500\n\n3. SOFTWARE\n   Grammarly: ₹10,000/year → 100% = ₹10,000\n   Google Workspace: ₹8,000/year → 100% = ₹8,000\n   Canva Pro: ₹5,000/year → 100% = ₹5,000\n\n4. PROFESSIONAL DEVELOPMENT\n   Online writing course: ₹15,000 → 100% = ₹15,000\n   Business books: ₹8,000 → 100% = ₹8,000\n\n5. MARKETING\n   Website hosting: ₹5,000 → 100% = ₹5,000\n   LinkedIn Premium: ₹12,000 → 100% = ₹12,000\n   Business cards: ₹2,000 → 100% = ₹2,000\n\n6. OPERATIONS\n   Co-working space: ₹36,000 → 100% = ₹36,000\n   Client travel: ₹12,000 → 100% = ₹12,000\n   Office supplies: ₹5,000 → 100% = ₹5,000\n\n7. FINANCIAL\n   CA fees: ₹10,000 → 100% = ₹10,000\n   Bank charges: ₹3,000 → 100% = ₹3,000\n\nTOTAL DEDUCTIONS: ₹2,26,100",
