        "title": "Expense Deductions — Kitna Bacha Sakte Ho (Part 2)",
        "content": "TAXABLE INCOME: ₹10,00,000 - ₹2,26,100 = ₹7,73,900\n\nNow, Rahul has choice:\nOption A: Claim actual expenses (₹2,26,100 deduction)\nOption B: Use 44ADA (50% of ₹10L = ₹5,00,000 deduction)\n\n44ADA gives MORE deduction (₹5,00,000 > ₹2,26,100)\nSo Rahul should use 44ADA!\n\nTaxable under 44ADA: ₹5,00,000\nTax (New Regime): ₹10,000 (approx)\nTax (Old Regime with 80C etc.): ₹7,500 (approx)\n\nRahul saves ₹2,500 by using Old Regime + 44ADA!\n```\n\n**Key Lesson:** Always compare actual expenses vs 44ADA. Whichever gives more deduction, use that!\n\n### Deep Dive: Depreciation Rules for Freelancers\n\nDepreciation samajhna zaroori hai kyunki expensive equipment ka poora expense ek saal mein claim nahi kar sakte — government kehti hai ki use and tear ke hisaab se claim karo.\n\n**Depreciation Rates (Income Tax Act):**\n\n| Asset | Depreciation Rate | Useful Life | Method |\n|-------|-------------------|-------------|--------|\n| Computers/Laptops | 40% | 3 years | WDV |\n| Software | 40% | 3 years | WDV |\n| Phones/Tablets | 40% | 3 years | WDV |\n| Cameras | 40% | 3 years | WDV |\n| Furniture | 10% | 10 years | WDV |\n| Office Equipment | 15% | 7 years | WDV |\n| Vehicles | 15% | 7 years | WDV |\n\n**WDV = Written Down Value** — matlab har saal remaining value pe depreciation lagta hai.\n\n**Depreciation Calculation Example:**\n\n```\nSneha ne 2024 mein ₹80,000 ka camera kharida\n\nYear 1 (2024-25): \nOpening Value: ₹80,000\nDepreciation: 40% of ₹80,000 = ₹32,000\nClosing Value: ₹48,000\n\nYear 2 (2025-26):\nOpening Value: ₹48,000\nDepreciation: 40% of ₹48,000 = ₹19,200\nClosing Value: ₹28,800\n\nYear 3 (2026-27):\nOpening Value: ₹28,800\nDepreciation: 40% of ₹28,800 = ₹11,520\nClosing Value: ₹17,280\n\nTotal Depreciation Claimed: ₹32,000 + ₹19,200 + ₹11,520 = ₹62,720\n```\n\n**Important Points:**\n1. Asset ka proof chahiye (invoice, bank statement)\n- Business use percentage calculate karo\n- Agar 50% personal + 50% business hai, toh sirf 50% depreciation claim karo\n- Asset sell karne pe, profit ya loss calculate hota hai\n\n### Home Office Deduction — Detailed Calculation\n\nFreelancers jo ghar se kaam karte hain, unke liye home office deduction bahut valuable hai. Lekin rules follow karo!\n\n**Calculation Method:**\n\n```\nStep 1: Total Area of Home\nExample: 1000 sq ft apartment\n\nStep 2: Area Used for Work\nExample: Dedicated office room = 150 sq ft\n\nStep 3: Calculate Percentage\n150/1000 = 15%\n\nStep 4: Apply to Relevant Expenses\nRent: ₹24,000/month × 12 = ₹2,88,000 × 15% = ₹43,200\nElectricity: ₹3,000/month × 12 = ₹36,000 × 15% = ₹5,400\nInternet: ₹1,200/month × 12 = ₹14,400 × 100% = ₹14,400 (fully used for work)\nWater: ₹500/month × 12 = ₹6,000 × 15% = ₹900\nMaintenance: ₹2,000/month × 12 = ₹24,000 × 15% = ₹3,600\n\nTotal Home Office Deduction: ₹67,500\n```\n\n**Conditions for Home Office Deduction:**\n1. Dedicated space hona chahiye (not shared with personal use)\n- Regularly aur exclusively business ke liye use hona chahiye\n- Self-employed hone chahiye (salaried ke liye alag rules hain)\n- Rent agreement mein name hona chahiye (if rented)\n- Property tax receipts (if owned)\n\n**Meera's Home Office Setup:**\n```\nMeera lives in a 2BHK apartment (900 sq ft)\nShe converted one bedroom into office (120 sq ft)",
