        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "TDS Claiming Aur Refund Process — Paisa Wapas Kaise Lein (Part 2)",
        "content": "**Kunal's Refund Problem:**\nKunal filed ITR, but refund didn't come for 6 months. Reason: He didn't verify ITR! After verification, refund came in 2 weeks. Lesson: Always verify ITR within 30 days!\n\n### Real Example: ₹50,000 TDS Deducted\n\n**Aman's Complete TDS Refund Calculation:**\n\n```\nAMAN WEB DEVELOPMENT\nFY 2025-26\n\nCLIENT PAYMENTS:\nClient A: ₹2,00,000 (TDS: ₹20,000)\nClient B: ₹1,50,000 (TDS: ₹15,000)\nClient C: ₹1,00,000 (TDS: ₹10,000)\nPlatform: ₹50,000 (TDS: ₹5,000)\nTotal Income: ₹5,00,000\nTotal TDS: ₹50,000\n\nTAX CALCULATION (44ADA):\nGross Receipts: ₹5,00,000\n50% Deduction: ₹2,50,000\nTaxable Income: ₹2,50,000\n\nTax (New Regime):\nUp to ₹3L: NIL\nTax: ₹0\nCess: ₹0\nTotal Tax: ₹0\n\nTAX LIABILITY: ₹0\nTDS DEDUCTED: ₹50,000\nREFUND: ₹50,000!\n\nAman gets full ₹50,000 back!\n```\n\n**Aman's Smart Move:** Aman invests his TDS refund every year in ELSS. In 5 years, ₹2.5 lakh refund + 12% returns = ₹3.75 lakh! Paisa paisa karta hai!\n\n### TDS on Different Types of Freelance Income\n\nHar type ke income pe alag TDS rules hain. Samajh lo, toh surprise nahi hoga!\n\n**Detailed TDS Rate Chart:**\n\n| Section | Nature of Payment | TDS Rate | Threshold (Single) | Threshold (Annual) | When to Deduct |\n|---------|-------------------|----------|--------------------|--------------------|----------------|\n| 194C | Contract work (Individual) | 1% | ₹30,000 | ₹1,00,000 | Payment credit/entry |\n| 194C | Contract work (Others) | 2% | ₹30,000 | ₹1,00,000 | Payment credit/entry |\n| 194J | Professional services | 10% | ₹30,000 | ₹30,000 | Payment credit/entry |\n| 194J | Technical services | 2% | ₹30,000 | ₹30,000 | Payment credit/entry |\n| 194H | Commission/brokerage | 5% | ₹15,000 | ₹15,000 | Payment credit/entry |\n| 194I(a) | Plant & machinery rent | 2% | ₹2,40,000 | ₹2,40,000 | Payment credit/entry |\n| 194I(b) | Land/building rent | 10% | ₹2,40,000 | ₹2,40,000 | Payment credit/entry |\n| 194A | Interest (other than bank) | 10% | ₹5,000 | ₹5,000 | Payment credit/entry |\n\n**Real-Life TDS Scenarios:**\n\n```\nScenario 1: Rahul designs a logo for ₹25,000\nSection: 194J (professional services)\nTDS Rate: 10%\nTDS: ₹2,500\nRahul receives: ₹22,500\n\nScenario 2: Priya writes 10 articles for ₹50,000\nSection: 194J (professional services)\nTDS Rate: 10%\nTDS: ₹5,000\nPriya receives: ₹45,000\n\nScenario 3: Kunal develops website for ₹1,50,000\nSection: 194J (professional services)\nTDS Rate: 10%\nTDS: ₹15,000\nKunal receives: ₹1,35,000\n\nScenario 4: Meera provides design retainer for ₹30,000/month\nSection: 194J (professional services)\nTDS Rate: 10%\nMonthly TDS: ₹3,000\nMeera receives: ₹27,000\n```\n\n### TDS Certificate — Form 16A\n\nJab client TDS kaata hai, toh use TDS certificate dena hota hai — Form 16A. Yeh tumhare liye proof hai ki TDS deducted hua hai.\n\n**Form 16A Details:**\n\n| Field | What It Contains |\n|-------|------------------|\n| Deductor | Client ka naam, PAN, TAN |\n| Deductee | Tumhara naam, PAN |\n| Income | Payment amount |\n| TDS Deducted | Kitna TDS kaata |\n| Date | Deduction ki date |\n| BSR Code | Bank ka code |\n| Challan Number | Government deposit proof |\n\n**How to Get Form 16A:**\n1. Client se directly request karo\n2. TRACES website se download karo (traces.gov.in)\n3. Client ke TDS return se generate hota hai\n\n**Common Issue:** Bohot se clients Form 16A nahi dete. Iska solution:\n- Email karo requesting certificate\n- Remind them it's their legal obligation\n- If they refuse, complain to Income Tax Department\n- Keep payment proof (bank statement, invoices)\n\n### TDS Credit Mismatch — Kya Karein?\n\nKabhi kabhi Form 26AS mein TDS credit nahi dikhta. Yeh common problem hai!\n\n**Reasons for Mismatch:**",
