        "id": "13-6-3",
        "topicId": "13-6",
        "topicTitle": "TDS Claiming Aur Refund Process — Paisa Wapas Kaise Lein",
        "cardIndex": 3,
        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "TDS Claiming Aur Refund Process — Paisa Wapas Kaise Lein (Part 3)",
        "content": "| Problem | Solution |\n|---------|----------|\n| Client ne TDS deposit nahi kiya | Client ko remind karo, legal notice bhejo |\n| Wrong PAN provided | Client se correction karo |\n| TDS return filed late | Wait for next quarter update |\n| Duplicate entry | Verify with client's TDS return |\n| Name mismatch | Update PAN details |\n\n**Sneha's TDS Mismatch Problem:**\n```\nSneha ne 3 clients se kaam kiya:\nClient A: ₹50,000 (TDS ₹5,000) - Credit dikh raha hai ✅\nClient B: ₹40,000 (TDS ₹4,000) - Credit nahi dikh raha ❌\nClient C: ₹60,000 (TDS ₹6,000) - Credit dikh raha hai ✅\n\nSolution:\n1. Client B ko email kiya with payment proof\n2. Client ne TDS return file nahi ki thi\n3. Client ne next quarter mein file kiya\n4. Sneha ko 3 months baad credit mila\n\nLesson: Har client se Form 16A maango!\n```\n\n### TDS Adjustment Against Advance Tax\n\nAgar tumhe TDS deducted hai, toh usse advance tax mein adjust kar sakte ho. Yeh smart tax planning hai!\n\n**Calculation Example:**\n\n```\nKunal's Tax Situation:\nTotal Expected Income: ₹12,00,000\nTax Liability (after deductions): ₹90,000\n\nTDS Deducted by Clients:\nClient A: ₹20,000\nClient B: ₹15,000\nClient C: ₹10,000\nTotal TDS: ₹45,000\n\nAdvance Tax Payable: ₹90,000 - ₹45,000 = ₹45,000\n\nInstallment Schedule:\nJune 15: 15% of ₹45,000 = ₹6,750\nSeptember 15: 30% of ₹45,000 = ₹13,500\nDecember 15: 30% of ₹45,000 = ₹13,500\nMarch 15: 25% of ₹45,000 = ₹11,250\nTotal: ₹45,000\n```\n\n**Important Notes:**\n1. TDS credit Form 26AS se verify karo\n- Advance tax installments mein TDS adjust mat karo (seedha final calculation mein)\n- Agar TDS zyada hai, toh refund milega\n- Agar advance tax kam hai, toh interest lagega\n\n### TDS Refund — Step-by-Step Process\n\n**Step 1: File ITR**\n- Login to incometax.gov.in\n- Select correct ITR form\n- Fill income and TDS details\n- Calculate tax liability\n- Claim refund\n\n**Step 2: Verify ITR**\n- Aadhaar OTP\n- Net banking\n- Physical verification (sending ITR-V to CPC)\n\n**Step 3: Wait for Processing**\n- CPC processes your return\n- Checks TDS credit\n- Calculates refund\n\n**Step 4: Refund Initiation**\n- Refund order generated\n- Sent to bank via ECS/NEFT\n- Takes 2-4 weeks\n\n**Step 5: Refund Credited**\n- Money in your bank account\n- SMS/email notification\n- Check bank statement\n\n**Timeline:**\n\n| Stage | Duration | What Happens |\n|-------|----------|--------------|\n| ITR Filing | Day 0 | You submit return |\n| Verification | Within 30 days | Must verify or return invalid |\n| Processing | 1-3 months | CPC checks everything |\n| Refund Order | 1-2 weeks after processing | Order generated |\n| Bank Credit | 1-2 weeks after order | Money in account |\n| Total | 2-5 months | From filing to credit |\n\n**Track Your Refund:**\n- Login to incometax.gov.in\n- Go to \"View Refund Status\"\n- Or use TIN-NSLC website\n- Enter PAN and assessment year\n\n### International Freelancing and TDS\n\nAgar tum foreign clients se kaam karte ho, toh TDS rules alag hain!\n\n**Key Points:**\n\n| Situation | TDS Applicable? | Why? |\n|-----------|----------------|------|\n| Indian client pays you | Yes (194J/194C) | Domestic payment |\n| Foreign client pays to Indian bank | No TDS | No Indian deductor |\n| Foreign client via Indian platform | Platform deducts TDS | Platform is deductor |\n| Foreign client via PayPal/Wise | No TDS | No Indian entity |\n\n**Example:**\n```\nAman works for US client directly:\nPayment: $5,000 (₹4,15,000)\nTDS Deducted: ₹0 (US client doesn't deduct Indian TDS)\nAman receives: ₹4,15,000\n\nBut Aman must:\n1. Report full income in ITR\n2. Pay advance tax if applicable\n3. File LUT for zero-rated supply (if registered for GST)\n```\n\n---",
