        "cardIndex": 3,
        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Invoice Management Aur Cash Flow Planning (Part 3)",
        "content": "### Emergency Fund for Freelancers\n\n| Monthly Expenses | Emergency Fund Needed | Months Covered |\n|-----------------|----------------------|----------------|\n| ₹30,000 | ₹2,70,000 - ₹3,60,000 | 9-12 months |\n| ₹50,000 | ₹4,50,000 - ₹6,00,000 | 9-12 months |\n| ₹75,000 | ₹6,75,000 - ₹9,00,000 | 9-12 months |\n| ₹1,00,000 | ₹9,00,000 - ₹12,00,000 | 9-12 months |\n\n**Why 9-12 months for freelancers?**\n- Income is irregular\n- Client payments delayed\n- Seasonal fluctuations\n- No paid leaves\n- No employer benefits\n\n### Cash Flow Forecasting\n\n**Monthly Cash Flow Template:**\n\n```\nCASH FLOW FORECAST - [MONTH]\n\nOPENING BALANCE: ₹_______\n\nINFLOWS:\nClient A (due 15th): ₹_______\nClient B (due 20th): ₹_______\nPlatform payment: ₹_______\nOther income: ₹_______\nTOTAL INFLOWS: ₹_______\n\nOUTFLOWS:\nRent: ₹_______\nGroceries: ₹_______\nUtilities: ₹_______\nSoftware subscriptions: ₹_______\nTax payment: ₹_______\nInsurance premium: ₹_______\nEMI/Loans: ₹_______\nMiscellaneous: ₹_______\nTOTAL OUTFLOWS: ₹_______\n\nNET CASH FLOW: ₹_______\nCLOSING BALANCE: ₹_______\n```\n\n### Client Payment Tracking System\n\n**Simple Google Sheet:**\n\n| Invoice # | Client | Amount | Date Sent | Due Date | Status | Days Overdue |\n|-----------|--------|--------|-----------|----------|--------|--------------|\n| PRI/042 | ABC Corp | ₹50,740 | 15-Jul | 14-Aug | Pending | 0 |\n| PRI/041 | XYZ Ltd | ₹35,000 | 01-Jul | 31-Jul | Paid | - |\n| PRI/040 | DEF Inc | ₹25,000 | 15-Jun | 15-Jul | Paid | - |\n| PRI/039 | GHI Co | ₹40,000 | 01-Jun | 01-Jul | Overdue | 45 days |\n\n**Payment Status Color Code:**\n- Green: Paid\n- Yellow: Due soon (within 7 days)\n- Orange: Overdue (1-30 days)\n- Red: Seriously overdue (30+ days)\n\n### When to Say No to Late-Paying Clients\n\n**Red Flags:**\n1. Client has history of 60+ day payments\n2. Client asks for 90+ day terms\n3. Client disputes invoices frequently\n4. Client pays only after multiple follow-ups\n5. Client asks for free work \"for exposure\"\n\n**Kunal's Rule:**\n\"Agar client ne 3 baar se zyada late pay kiya hai, main uske saath kaam nahi karta. Time = Money, aur main dono waste nahi karunga!\"\n\n**Alternative:**\n- Take 50% advance from late-paying clients\n- Use milestone payments for large projects\n- Set clear payment terms in contract\n- Charge late fees (1.5-2% per month)\n\n---",
