        "title": "Freelancer Tax Calendar — Poora Saal Ka Schedule (Part 3)",
        "content": "Agar tum abhi freelancing start kar rahe ho, toh yeh 10 steps follow karo:\n\n**Step 1: Get PAN Card**\n- Agar nahi hai, turant apply karo\n- Online apply: incometax.gov.in\n- Fee: ₹107 (NSDL)\n- Time: 15-20 days\n\n**Step 2: Open Business Bank Account**\n- Current account opening\n- Separate from personal account\n- Easy income tracking\n- Professional image\n\n**Step 3: Set Up Expense Tracking**\n- Google Sheet ya app (Wave, Zoho)\n- Har receipt photograph karo\n- Monthly categorize karo\n- Cloud backup rakho\n\n**Step 4: Get Health Insurance**\n- Age 22-25: ₹5-10 lakh coverage\n- Premium: ₹5,000-12,000/year\n- Tax benefit under 80D\n- Emergency protection\n\n**Step 5: Start Retirement Investment**\n- Open NPS account\n- Start ELSS SIP\n- Open PPF account\n- Minimum ₹5,000/month total\n\n**Step 6: Set Up Invoicing**\n- Professional invoice template\n- GST details (if registered)\n- Payment terms clear\n- Follow-up system\n\n**Step 7: Understand GST**\n- Income < ₹20 lakh: Optional\n- Income > ₹20 lakh: Mandatory\n- GST rates: 18% on services\n- ITC benefits\n\n**Step 8: Learn About Advance Tax**\n- Annual income > ₹10 lakh: Mandatory\n- Due dates: June 15, Sep 15, Dec 15, Mar 15\n- 15%, 45%, 75%, 100% installments\n- Interest for late payment\n\n**Step 9: Find a Good CA**\n- ICAI website se dhundho\n- Friend referrals lo\n- Annual fee: ₹10,000-25,000\n- Worth it for tax savings\n\n**Step 10: Build Emergency Fund**\n- 9-12 months expenses\n- Separate savings account\n- Liquid funds for better returns\n- Don't touch for regular expenses\n\n---",
